exports[`R7 — capability digest v2 snapshot test digest markdown matches snapshot (changes only when registry does) 1`] = `
"# Slide block capabilities

Generated from the live block library and slide layouts — do not hand-author a copy of this document, it will drift. Every block below is a closed vocabulary entry: pick a \`type\`, fill its declared slots, and never invent a region name, a slot, or a coordinate.

## Color roles

Use role names (e.g. \`accent\`, \`text\`) in slot values — never bare hex.

- **surface**: Default background fill; resolved from theme.
- **surfaceAlt**: Slightly tinted surface for alternating rows or cards.
- **accent**: Primary brand accent for buttons, links, highlights.
- **accent2**: Secondary accent for charts, secondary emphasis.
- **text**: Primary text colour; contrast-solved against the surface (≥ 4.5:1).
- **textMuted**: Secondary text colour for captions, footnotes; contrast-solved (≥ 4.5:1).
- **positive**: Green status colour for growth, success, positive deltas.
- **negative**: Red status colour for decline, errors, negative deltas.
- **warning**: Amber status colour for caution, in-progress, mixed results.
- **neutral**: Grey status colour for neutral or unavailable data.
- **line**: Hairlines, dividers, gridlines; contrast-solved (≥ 1.4:1).
- **scrim**: Dark overlay for text over images; semi-transparent black wash.

## Style

BlockStyleSpec fields (all optional; absent = theme default):

- \`surface: ColorRole | string — block background\`
- \`on: ColorRole | string — foreground colour (derived from surface when absent)\`
- \`accent: ColorRole | string — emphasis colour\`
- \`tone: 'filled' | 'outline' | 'ghost' | 'inverted' | 'gradient' — visual tone\`
- \`radius: RadiusToken | number — corner radius (none | sm | md | lg | xl | pill)\`
- \`padding: SpaceToken | number | [number, number] — inner padding\`
- \`gap: SpaceToken | number — gap between children\`
- \`elevation: 0 | 1 | 2 — shadow level\`
- \`align: 'start' | 'center' | 'end' — content alignment\`
- \`density: 'compact' | 'default' | 'roomy' — visual compactness\`

Gradient shape: \`Paint: { type: 'solid', color } | { type: 'linearGradient', angle, stops: [{color, at}] } | { type: 'radialGradient', cx, cy, stops: [{color, at}] }\`

## Motion

Set \`motion.preset\` on any block. Every preset below plays (no-op excluded).

- **fade** _text-reveal_ — 250ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **fade-up** _text-reveal_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **fade-down** _text-reveal_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **pop** _badge_ — 250ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **wipe-x** _panel-reveal_ — 350ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **wipe-y** _panel-reveal_ — 350ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **mask-reveal** _panel-reveal_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **reveal-down** _text-reveal_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **stagger-lines** _text-reveal_ — 500ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick, stagger 40ms
- **stagger-children** _text-reveal_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick, stagger 40ms
- **stagger-grid** _text-reveal_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick, stagger 40ms
- **words-in** _text-reveal_ — 500ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick, stagger 40ms
- **quote-in** _composite_ — 1000ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: pop → stagger-lines → fade)
- **count-up** _card-resize_ — 500ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **grow-bars-x** _card-resize_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick, stagger 40ms
- **grow-bars-y** _card-resize_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick, stagger 40ms
- **grow-segments** _card-resize_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick, stagger 40ms
- **draw-path** _success-check_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **draw-axis-then-nodes** _success-check_ — 800ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: draw-path → stagger-children)
- **sweep** _success-check_ — 500ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **sweep-nodes** _text-reveal_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick, stagger 40ms
- **pop-points** _badge_ — 250ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick, stagger 40ms
- **radiate** _composite_ — 650ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: pop → stagger-children)
- **grow-branches** _success-check_ — 800ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: draw-path → stagger-children)
- **split-in** _text-reveal_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **field-in** _text-reveal_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **title-then-body** _composite_ — 650ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: fade-up → fade)
- **title-then-split** _composite_ — 800ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: fade-up → split-in)
- **scrim-then-text** _composite_ — 750ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: fade → stagger-lines)
- **ken-burns** _ambient_ — 500ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (loops)
- **cover-in** _composite_ — 1400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: fade → words-in → fade-up → fade)
- **section-in** _composite_ — 1000ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: pop → wipe-x → fade-up)
- **dashboard-in** _composite_ — 800ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: stagger-children → grow-bars-y)
- **closing-in** _composite_ — 650ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: fade-up → pop)

## Layouts

Region names belong to the layout — pick a \`layout\`, then only use the regions it lists.

| Layout | Regions | Use when |
|---|---|---|
| \`title\` (Title) | \`title\`, \`subtitle\` | Centered title + subtitle, ideal for simple title slides. |
| \`section\` (Section) | \`title\`, \`subtitle\` | Large title + small subtitle for section dividers. |
| \`two-column\` (Two Column) | \`title\`, \`left\`, \`right\` | Left/right split with a title bar — the workhorse layout. |
| \`three-column\` (Three Column) | \`title\`, \`a\`, \`b\`, \`c\` | Equal thirds with a title bar — comparison or feature lists. |
| \`four-up\` (Four Up) | \`title\`, \`q1\`, \`q2\`, \`q3\`, \`q4\` | 2×2 grid with a title bar — feature matrices, quadrants. |
| \`image-left\` (Image Left) | \`title\`, \`image\`, \`text\` | Image (60%) left, text (40%) right — photo + caption. |
| \`image-right\` (Image Right) | \`title\`, \`text\`, \`image\` | Text (40%) left, image (60%) right — text-first image support. |
| \`image-top\` (Image Top) | \`title\`, \`image\`, \`text\` | Image (60%) top, text (40%) bottom — hero image layout. |
| \`image-bottom\` (Image Bottom) | \`title\`, \`text\`, \`image\` | Text (40%) top, image (60%) bottom — caption-over-image. |
| \`grid-3x2\` (Grid 3×2) | \`title\`, \`c1\`, \`c2\`, \`c3\`, \`c4\`, \`c5\`, \`c6\` | 3 columns × 2 rows — gallery, feature cards. |
| \`grid-2x3\` (Grid 2×3) | \`title\`, \`a\`, \`b\`, \`c\`, \`d\`, \`e\`, \`f\` | 2 columns × 3 rows — compact data grid. |
| \`comparison\` (Comparison) | \`title\`, \`left\`, \`right\` | Two equal columns for side-by-side comparison. |
| \`timeline\` (Timeline) | \`title\`, \`timeline\` | Full-width horizontal timeline area with title. |
| \`quote\` (Quote) | \`quote\`, \`attribution\` | Narrowed centered quote with attribution — testimonial slides. |
| \`kpi-row\` (KPI Row) | \`title\`, \`kpi1\`, \`kpi2\`, \`kpi3\`, \`kpi4\` | Title + 4 equal KPI cells — dashboard-style metrics. |
| \`blank\` (Blank) | \`content\` | Single content region, full safe area — maximum flexibility. |

## Blocks

### \`tls.c.agenda\` — Agenda

Agenda or table-of-contents slide. Numbered items with titles and optional notes. Use 3–8 items. Highlight the current topic with the \`current\` prop. _(family: composite; keywords: agenda, toc, table of contents, outline, topics, schedule, items)_

**When:** Use for a table-of-contents or agenda slide listing 3–8 topics. Set \`current\` to highlight the active topic.
**Avoid:** Do not use for more than 8 items — split into two sections. Do not use for a timeline (use tls.g.timeline-h).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`items\` | yes | list of object (title, note) (1–12 items) | 3–8 items. Each title should be 1–6 words. Notes are optional and brief. |
| \`current\` | no | number | Index of the currently highlighted item (0-based). Omit or set to null to highlight none. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_agenda\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.agenda\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"items\\": [
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Opening\\",
        \\"note\\": \\"Welcome and agenda overview\\"
      },
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Q3 Results\\",
        \\"note\\": \\"Revenue and growth metrics\\"
      },
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Strategy\\",
        \\"note\\": \\"Next quarter priorities\\"
      },
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Q&A\\",
        \\"note\\": \\"Questions and discussion\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"current\\": 1
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.big-stat\` — Big Stat [html]

Big number slide. One enormous headline metric with a short label and optional context line. Use for KPIs, milestones, and hero stats. _(family: composite; keywords: stat, big, number, kpi, metric, hero, headline, count)_

**When:** Use for a single hero statistic — one big number with a label and optional context.
**Avoid:** Do not use for multiple metrics side by side — use tls.c.kpi-row instead.

**Parts:** \`value\`, \`label\`, \`context\`

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`value\` | yes | number | The headline number to display. Any numeric value. |
| \`label\` | yes | text (max 40 chars) | Short label describing the number. 1–4 words, e.g. \\"Total Revenue\\". |
| \`context\` | no | text (max 60 chars) | Optional supporting line below the label (e.g. \\"vs last quarter\\"). |
| \`format\` | no | enum: plain \\\\| compact \\\\| percent \\\\| currency | Number format: plain (default), compact (1.2K/3.4M), percent (12%), currency (1,234). |
| \`prefix\` | no | text (max 4 chars) | Optional prefix before the number (e.g. \\"$\\", \\"€\\"). Max 4 chars. |
| \`suffix\` | no | text (max 4 chars) | Optional suffix after the number (e.g. \\"%\\", \\"M\\"). Max 4 chars. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_big_stat\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.big-stat\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"value\\": 4200000,
    \\"label\\": \\"Total Revenue\\",
    \\"context\\": \\"vs last quarter\\",
    \\"format\\": \\"compact\\",
    \\"prefix\\": \\"$\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.comparison\` — Comparison

Side-by-side comparison of 2–3 columns, each with a title and a list of items. Use to contrast options, plans, or viewpoints. Highlight the recommended column with the \`highlight\` prop. _(family: composite; keywords: comparison, versus, compare, columns, side by side, options, contrast, pros, cons, alternatives)_

**When:** Use to compare 2–3 options, plans, or viewpoints side by side. Set \`highlight\` to draw attention to the recommended column.
**Avoid:** Do not use for more than 3 columns — split into two slides. Do not use for sequential processes — use tls.c.steps.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`columns\` | yes | list of object (title, items) (2–3 items) | 2–3 columns, each with a short title (2–6 words) and 2–6 short items (2–8 words each). |
| \`highlight\` | no | number | Index (0-based) of the column to highlight with accent colour. Omit or null for none. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_comparison\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.comparison\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"columns\\": [
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Build In-House\\",
        \\"items\\": [
          \\"Full control\\",
          \\"Higher upfront cost\\",
          \\"Longer timeline\\"
        ]
      },
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Buy SaaS\\",
        \\"items\\": [
          \\"Quick setup\\",
          \\"Lower upfront cost\\",
          \\"Vendor lock-in risk\\"
        ]
      },
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Hybrid\\",
        \\"items\\": [
          \\"Balanced approach\\",
          \\"Moderate cost\\",
          \\"Flexible roadmap\\"
        ]
      }
    ],
    \\"highlight\\": 2
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.feature-grid\` — Feature Grid [html]

Grid of feature cells, each with an icon, title, and description. 2–6 cells arranged in 2/3/4 columns. _(family: composite; keywords: feature, grid, capabilities, benefits, icon, tiles, services, highlights)_

**When:** Use to show 2–6 feature highlights in a grid layout — each cell has an icon, title, and short description. Good for capability overviews, service lists, or product feature showcases.
**Avoid:** Do not use for single-row comparisons (use tls.c.comparison) or for more than 6 items (use tls.c.agenda or tls.c.steps).

**Parts:** \`cell[*].icon\`, \`cell[*].title\`, \`cell[*].desc\`

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`cells\` | yes | list of object (icon, title, desc) (2–6 items) | List of 2–6 feature cells, each with icon (icon id string), title (short, 1–4 words), and desc (one sentence). Describe features, benefits, or capabilities. |
| \`columns\` | no | number (min 2, max 4) | Number of columns: 2, 3, or 4. Default is 3. |
| \`gap\` | no | number (min 8, max 48) | Gap between cells in slide units. Default 24. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_feature_grid\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.feature-grid\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"cells\\": [
      {
        \\"icon\\": \\"zap\\",
        \\"title\\": \\"Fast\\",
        \\"desc\\": \\"Optimised for speed at every layer.\\"
      },
      {
        \\"icon\\": \\"shield\\",
        \\"title\\": \\"Secure\\",
        \\"desc\\": \\"End-to-end encryption by default.\\"
      },
      {
        \\"icon\\": \\"globe\\",
        \\"title\\": \\"Global\\",
        \\"desc\\": \\"Deployed across 30+ regions.\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"columns\\": 3,
    \\"gap\\": 24
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.hero\` — Hero [html]

Opening slide. One idea in the title, no full sentence; subtitle gives date/audience; CTA optional. _(family: composite; keywords: hero, opening, title, cover, splash, intro, landing)_

**When:** Use as a title/cover slide — one idea in the title, date/audience in the subtitle. Pick variant \\"classic\\" for a standard hero, \\"split\\" when you want the title to reveal from two halves sliding in from opposite sides, or \\"gradient-sweep\\" for a decorative background gradient that sweeps in behind the title on reveal.
**Avoid:** Do not use for content slides that have data or body text — use tls.t.title.

**Parts:** \`kicker\`, \`title\`, \`subtitle\`, \`cta\`

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`kicker\` | no | text (max 60 chars) | Short label above the title: section name, category, or status. 1–4 words. |
| \`title\` | yes | richText (max 120 chars) | A concise slide title. Bold one key word for emphasis. Never a full sentence. Max 120 chars. |
| \`subtitle\` | no | richText | Supporting line: date, audience, or context. 3–12 words. |
| \`cta\` | no | text (max 40 chars) | Optional button text. Short imperative, 2–4 words. |
| \`variant\` | no | enum: classic \\\\| split \\\\| gradient-sweep | Visual style: \\"classic\\" (default) standard hero with staggered part reveal; \\"split\\" split-title reveal where halves slide in from opposite sides; \\"gradient-sweep\\" a decorative gradient sweeps in behind the title on reveal. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_hero\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.hero\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"kicker\\": \\"QUARTERLY REVIEW\\",
    \\"title\\": {
      \\"runs\\": [
        {
          \\"text\\": \\"Margin fell on \\"
        },
        {
          \\"text\\": \\"infrastructure\\",
          \\"bold\\": true
        }
      ]
    },
    \\"subtitle\\": {
      \\"runs\\": [
        {
          \\"text\\": \\"Q3 FY2026\\"
        }
      ]
    },
    \\"cta\\": \\"\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.image-text\` — Image + text

Image beside or above a text cluster (kicker + title + body). Configurable placement and image ratio. _(family: composite; keywords: image, text, photo, picture, editorial, side-by-side, layout, composite)_

**When:** Use when a slide needs an image alongside or above explanatory text — editorial layouts, feature descriptions, team slides.
**Avoid:** Do not use for image-only slides — use tls.m.image. Do not use for text-only slides — use tls.t.title + tls.t.body.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`image\` | yes | image | Asset id or URL of the image to display beside or above the text. |
| \`alt\` | yes | text (max 200 chars) | 1–10 words describing what the image shows. |
| \`placement\` | no | enum: left \\\\| right \\\\| top | Where the image sits relative to the text cluster. |
| \`imageRatio\` | no | number (min 0.2, max 0.8) | Fraction of the box given to the image (left/right splits width, top splits height). |
| \`kicker\` | no | text (max 60 chars) | Short label above the title: section name, category, or status. 1–4 words. |
| \`title\` | yes | text (max 120 chars) | A concise slide title. 3–10 words. Never a full sentence. |
| \`body\` | no | text (max 500 chars) | 1–3 sentences of supporting body copy. |
| \`gutter\` | no | enum: xs \\\\| sm \\\\| md \\\\| lg \\\\| xl | Gap between the image and the text cluster. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_image_text\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.image-text\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"image\\": \\"hero-photo\\",
    \\"alt\\": \\"Team meeting in conference room\\",
    \\"placement\\": \\"left\\",
    \\"kicker\\": \\"OVERVIEW\\",
    \\"title\\": \\"Our design process\\",
    \\"body\\": \\"We start with research, prototype rapidly, and validate with users before shipping.\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.kpi-row\` — KPI Row

Row of 2–5 KPI tiles with equal-width split. Each tile delegates to tls.c.kpi-tile. _(family: composite; keywords: kpi, row, tiles, dashboard, metrics, numbers, stats)_

**When:** Use to display 2–5 KPI metrics side-by-side in a row. Good for dashboards and summary slides.
**Avoid:** Do not use for a single KPI — use tls.c.kpi-tile. Do not use for more than 5 KPIs — split across slides.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`tiles\` | yes | list of object (value, delta, label, sparkline, polarity, format) (2–5 items) | 2–5 KPI tiles. Each needs a value and label. Use delta for change indicators and sparkline for trend. |
| \`gap\` | no | enum: xs \\\\| sm \\\\| md \\\\| lg | Horizontal spacing between tiles. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_kpi_row\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.kpi-row\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"tiles\\": [
      {
        \\"value\\": 4200000,
        \\"delta\\": 12.5,
        \\"label\\": \\"Revenue\\",
        \\"polarity\\": \\"upGood\\",
        \\"format\\": \\"compact\\"
      },
      {
        \\"value\\": 3.1,
        \\"delta\\": -0.8,
        \\"label\\": \\"Churn %\\",
        \\"polarity\\": \\"downGood\\",
        \\"format\\": \\"percent\\"
      },
      {
        \\"value\\": 892,
        \\"delta\\": 42,
        \\"label\\": \\"NPS\\",
        \\"polarity\\": \\"upGood\\",
        \\"format\\": \\"plain\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"gap\\": \\"md\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.kpi-tile\` — KPI Tile

Single KPI metric: headline number, change indicator, label, optional sparkline. Polarity-driven colour. _(family: composite; keywords: kpi, tile, metric, number, stat, value, delta, sparkline, dashboard)_

**When:** Use to display a single KPI metric with its value, change indicator, and optional trend line.
**Avoid:** Do not use for multiple KPIs side-by-side — use tls.c.kpi-row. Do not use for non-numeric hero text — use tls.t.title.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`value\` | yes | number (min -1000000000000, max 1000000000000) | The headline metric number. Use a plain number; formatting is applied by the block. |
| \`delta\` | no | number | Change indicator. Positive = improved, negative = declined (relative to polarity). |
| \`label\` | no | text (max 30 chars) | Metric name. 1–3 words, never a sentence. |
| \`sparkline\` | no | list of number (2–20 items) | 2–20 numbers for a mini trend line. Omit for a single-point metric. |
| \`polarity\` | no | enum: upGood \\\\| downGood | Which direction is \\"good\\". upGood = higher is better (revenue). downGood = lower is better (churn). |
| \`format\` | no | enum: plain \\\\| compact \\\\| percent \\\\| currency | Number formatting hint. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_kpi_tile\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.kpi-tile\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"value\\": 4200000,
    \\"delta\\": 12.5,
    \\"label\\": \\"Revenue\\",
    \\"polarity\\": \\"upGood\\",
    \\"format\\": \\"compact\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.steps\` — Steps

Process or timeline of numbered steps with titles and optional descriptions. Arranges steps horizontally or vertically with thin connectors between them. _(family: composite; keywords: steps, process, timeline, flow, workflow, sequential, phases, roadmap, numbered)_

**When:** Use to show a process, workflow, or timeline with 2–8 numbered steps that the audience reads in sequence.
**Avoid:** Do not use for a simple list of items — use tls.t.bullets. Do not use for fewer than 2 steps — use tls.t.title.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`steps\` | yes | list of object (title, desc) (1–12 items) | 2–6 steps, each 2–8 words in the title. Description is optional, 1–2 sentences. |
| \`orientation\` | no | enum: horizontal \\\\| vertical | Layout direction: horizontal (left to right) or vertical (top to bottom). |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_steps\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.steps\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"steps\\": [
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Plan\\",
        \\"desc\\": \\"Define scope and requirements\\"
      },
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Build\\",
        \\"desc\\": \\"Implement the solution\\"
      },
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Ship\\",
        \\"desc\\": \\"Deploy to production\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"orientation\\": \\"horizontal\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.testimonial\` — Testimonial [html]

Pull-quote testimonial with attribution. Quote text with speaker name, role, and optional avatar. Use for social proof, customer quotes, or endorsements. _(family: composite; keywords: testimonial, quote, pull-quote, endorsement, social-proof, attribution)_

**When:** Use for a customer quote, testimonial, or endorsement — quote text with speaker name, role, and optional avatar.
**Avoid:** Do not use for general block quotes or section dividers — use tls.t.title or a layout container.

**Parts:** \`quote\`, \`avatar\`, \`name\`, \`role\`

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`quote\` | yes | richText (max 500 chars) | The testimonial quote. 1–3 sentences. Bold key phrases for emphasis. |
| \`name\` | yes | text (max 60 chars) | Speaker's full name. 2–4 words. |
| \`role\` | yes | text (max 80 chars) | Speaker's title or position. 2–8 words. |
| \`avatar\` | no | text (max 200 chars) | Avatar image URL (https:) or asset id. Optional; shows initials when absent. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_testimonial\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.testimonial\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"quote\\": \\"This product transformed how our team works. We shipped 3× faster in the first quarter.\\",
    \\"name\\": \\"Jane Doe\\",
    \\"role\\": \\"VP of Engineering\\",
    \\"avatar\\": \\"\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.d.bar\` — Column Chart

Vertical column chart with zero baseline. _(family: data; keywords: chart, bar, column, data, graph, vertical)_

**When:** Use to compare values across categories — 1–20 bars, single series.
**Avoid:** Do not use for trends over time (use a line chart) or parts of a whole (use donut).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`categories\` | yes | list of text (1–20 items) | Category labels along the X axis. |
| \`series\` | yes | series of number (max 6) | Numeric values for each bar. Use null/NaN for missing data. |
| \`highlightIndex\` | no | number (min -1) | Index of the bar to highlight with accent color. -1 = none. |
| \`title\` | no | text (max 120 chars) | Chart title, shown above the chart area. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_bar\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.d.bar\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"categories\\": [
      \\"Q1\\",
      \\"Q2\\",
      \\"Q3\\"
    ],
    \\"series\\": [
      64,
      64,
      61
    ],
    \\"highlightIndex\\": 2,
    \\"title\\": \\"Revenue by Quarter\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.l.card\` — Card

Filled container with configurable padding. _(family: layout; keywords: card, container, padding, filled)_

**When:** Use to group children inside a visible, padded container.
**Avoid:** Do not use for transparent grouping — use tls.l.stack without style.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`padding\` | no | enum: 3xs \\\\| 2xs \\\\| xs \\\\| sm \\\\| md \\\\| lg \\\\| xl \\\\| 2xl \\\\| 3xl \\\\| 4xl | Inner padding of the card. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_card\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.l.card\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"padding\\": \\"md\\"
  },
  \\"children\\": []
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.l.field\` — Field

Full-bleed background fill. _(family: layout; keywords: field, background, fill, full-bleed)_

